# Secrets & security

- NEVER commit secrets or API keys. Use `.env` files; provide `.env.example` with placeholder values.
- Keep `.env`, `google-services*.json`, and `google-service-account.json` git-ignored.
- Known hardcoded secrets to remove/move (see `AGENT_PROMPT.md`):
  - `CustomerApp/environment.js` — Stripe public key, Google OAuth client IDs, Amplitude key.
  - `Admin Dashboard/src/index.js` — Firebase config and VAPID key.
  - `CustomerApp/app.json` / `RiderApp/app.json` — Google Maps API key.
- Do not introduce new hardcoded keys when refactoring.
- A pre-tool-use hook (`secret-guard.cjs`) blocks writing known secret patterns; honor it and move the value to `.env` instead.
